## Summary — AMSD-2041: Contentstack Live Preview

Built on the prior attempt's changes and completed the wiring so draft preview actually works end-to-end for this **CSR / Pages Router** app. Root mechanism (verified against the installed SDKs, not assumed): `ContentstackLivePreview.init` parses the URL `live_preview` hash and stamps it onto the shared `Stack.live_preview`; the delivery SDK then routes matching fetches to the preview host with `live_preview=<hash>`; `onEntryChange` fires with **no arguments** on each edit, so the app must re-fetch using the SDK-synced stack state.

### Files changed
- **`src/services/contentstack.ts`** (prior attempt, kept) — added `live_preview` block (`enable`, `host`, `management_token`) to `options` and client-side `ContentstackLivePreview.init` with the shared `Stack`.
- **`src/services/pageService.ts`** (this turn) — added `subscribeToLivePreview({ contentTypeUid, content, onContentUpdate })`: registers `ContentstackLivePreview.onEntryChange`, and on each change re-fetches the previewed entry's **draft** content via the prescribed **`getEntry`** helper (resolving the content-type from `ContentstackLivePreview.config.stackDetails.contentTypeUid` with fallbacks) and merges it into context. Guarded to client-side + preview-enabled only. Imports `pageService` types from `context/ContentstackContext`.
- **`src/context/ContentstackContext.tsx`** — replaced `useMemo` with `useState` + `updateContent` merge; added a `useEffect` that subscribes via `pageService.subscribeToLivePreview` so `ContentstackProvider` → `ContentstackContext` → `useContent` re-renders all 60+ consuming components with draft values. Exported `IContentstackContent` for the service.
- **`src/constants/publicEnv.ts`** (new this turn, not in the original list) — exposed `NEXT_PUBLIC_CONTENTSTACK_LIVE_PREVIEW` as `publicEnv.CONTENTSTACK_LIVE_PREVIEW`, because the preview re-fetch runs **client-side** where non-prefixed env vars are inlined/undefined in the browser bundle.
- **`.env.local`** — added the 4 live-preview keys (empty) so the pre-commit/env check has them.
- **`.env.local.sample`** — documented `CONTENTSTACK_LIVE_PREVIEW`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_CONTENTSTACK_LIVE_PREVIEW`, `CONTENTSTACK_LIVE_PREVIEW_TOKEN`, `CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST`, with comments noting preview URL patterns are configured in the Contentstack dashboard (Settings > Stack > Live Preview), not env vars.
- **`package.json`** (prior attempt, kept) — declared `@contentstack/live-preview-utils@^4.5.0`.

### Both prescribed helpers used
- **`getEntry`** → used in `pageService.subscribeToLivePreview` for the draft re-fetch.
- **`getValue`** → used to safely read `ContentstackLivePreview.config` and the page's locale/contentType from context.

### Not changed (and why)
- **`src/pages/_app.tsx`** — no edit needed; it already wraps the tree in `<ContentstackProvider defaultContent={content}>`, which now carries the live-preview subscription internally.
- **`src/hooks/useContent.ts`** — per the RCA, no structural change; it reads latest context via `useContentstackContext`, so it picks up draft updates automatically once the provider's state updates.
- **`src/interface/content/page.ts`** — no new types required; the wiring uses existing `IContentstackContent` / `IContentstackPage`.

